.TH CHTTPCLIENT_RESP_HEADER_AT 3 "2026-09-29" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpclient_resp_header_at \- get one occurrence of a response header
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpclient.h>

const char *chttpclient_resp_header_at(const chttpcli_response *resp,
                                       const char *name, size_t index);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function gives the value of one line of the response header
block with the name that you give; the lookup ignores the case of the
name. index counts the lines with that name, from 0, in the order in
which the server sent them. Each value is the value of one line exactly
as the server sent it, never a combined value.

chttpclient_resp_header_count gives the number of lines with a name,
and chttpclient_resp_header gives the combined value of a repeated
name, or the first value of a repeated Set-Cookie.

The pointer that the function gives back stays valid until a call to
chttpclient_resp_free.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
resp   The response to query. It can be NULL, and the function then
       gives NULL.
name   The header name. It can be NULL, and the function then gives
       NULL.
index  Which occurrence to give, from 0 to
       chttpclient_resp_header_count(resp, name) - 1.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A pointer to the value string of that occurrence, or NULL when index
is not below the number of lines with that name.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Only the header block of the response counts. A trailer field of a
chunked response body is not a response header, and this function
never gives one.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
size_t n = chttpclient_resp_header_count(resp, "Set-Cookie");
for (size_t i = 0; i < n; i++)
    printf("cookie: %s\\n",
           chttpclient_resp_header_at(resp, "Set-Cookie", i));
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpclient_resp_header_count (3),
.BR chttpclient_resp_header (3),
.BR chttpclient_resp_free (3)
